{"content":[{"c":["TOLA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of the four sons of Issachar named among the 66 descendants of Jacob who accompanied him in the migration to Egypt to join Joseph (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.13","r":"Gen.46.13","rawR":"Gen.46.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.13","value":"Gen.46.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:13"},"); and the ancestor of the first of four families of the tribe of Issachar, as identified in the census of Israel undertaken by Moses and Eleazar (",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.23","r":"Num.26.23","rawR":"Num.26.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.23","value":"Num.26.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 26:23"},"). Tola’s sons were Uzzi, Rephaiah, Jeriel, Jahmai, Ibsam, and Shemuel (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.2","r":"1Chr.7.2","rawR":"1Chr.7.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.2","value":"1Chr.7.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:2"},"). The Israelite clan of the Tolaites took its name from him (",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.23","r":"Num.26.23","rawR":"Num.26.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.23","value":"Num.26.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 26:23"},"), and during the time of David the warriors of his family numbered 22,600 men (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.1-2","r":"1Chr.7.1-2","rawR":"1Chr.7.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.1-2","value":"1Chr.7.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:1-2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of the judges of Israel, the son of Puah and the grandson of Dodo (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.10.1","r":"Judg.10.1","rawR":"Judg.10.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.10.1","value":"Judg.10.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 10:1"},"), of Issachar’s tribe. Shamir, his home and burial place, was in the hill country of Ephraim. There he judged Israel for 23 years."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["Although he “delivered” Israel after the debacle of Abimelech’s abortive attempt to establish a monarchy at Shechem, his accomplishment is covered in just two verses (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.10.1-2","r":"Judg.10.1-2","rawR":"Judg.10.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.10.1-2","value":"Judg.10.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 10:1-2"},"). Like other “minor judges,” mentioned only briefly (e.g., ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.12.8-15","r":"Judg.12.8-15","rawR":"Judg.12.8-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.12.8-15","value":"Judg.12.8-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:8-15"},"), he actually functioned in the judicial role—some more prominent “judges” (e.g., Gideon and Jephthah) were first, and perhaps solely, military heroes."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=JudgesBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JudgesBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JudgesBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Judges, Book of"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Tola","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 46:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.13","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.13","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.13"},{"anchorText":"Nm 26:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.26.23","rawQueryValue":"Num.26.23","sourceRefExact":"Num.26.23"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.2","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.2","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.2"},{"anchorText":"Nm 26:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.26.23","rawQueryValue":"Num.26.23","sourceRefExact":"Num.26.23"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:1-2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.1-2","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.1-2","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.1-2"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 10:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.10.1","rawQueryValue":"Judg.10.1","sourceRefExact":"Judg.10.1"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 10:1-2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.10.1-2","rawQueryValue":"Judg.10.1-2","sourceRefExact":"Judg.10.1-2"},{"anchorText":"12:8-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.12.8-15","rawQueryValue":"Judg.12.8-15","sourceRefExact":"Judg.12.8-15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"896c72ea1c66b821a852f9c40734445f86f3ed3ed74c313c2ee4af019e4220da","sourceItemName":"Tola","sourceItemOrder":201,"sourceMember":"Articles/T.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Tola","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Tola","title":"Tola","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}